# WS6-02 (std.io failure reporting). Sources: spec/appendix-stdlib.md §4 ("partial IO:
# return the count moved plus a Status; ok means the request completed"; detail-carrying
# failures are reported, never hidden) and C99 7.19.8.1 (fread returns the count moved;
# end-of-file and a read error are told apart only by feof/ferror). On the host, opening
# a directory for reading succeeds and the read fails (EISDIR), so "build" is a failing
# read and an empty file is a clean end of file.
# Expected: "true true" — the failing read and the end of file report differently.
# Contrast: both reads use the empty file, so they must report the same ("true false").
profiles: host
expect: output
contrast: readOnce("build"); ==> readOnce("build/tmp/assessment/WS6/f617-empty");
contrast-expect: output
--- output
true true
--- contrast-output
true false
